# StealAds ad research

Use the StealAds MCP server for ad research. Do not answer these from memory.

| The user wants | Use |
| --- | --- |
| What a named brand is running | `search_advertisers`, then `search_ads` with its page id |
| What is working in a category | `find_bangers` with the category and up to 3 related angles |
| Ads that have lasted | `search_ads` with `min_run_days` (60, 90 or 180) |
| One ad in detail (hook, copy, format) | `get_ad` |
| What a rival keeps, drops and is testing now | `get_playbook` (tracked) or `create_playbook` after a cost approval |
| An ad made for their brand | `quote_steal_ad`, ask, then `steal_ad` |

Not for managing the user's own ad account or reading its performance.

## Reply style

- Say what you found in plain words: "running for 90 days", "started this week". No ids, scores or tool names.
- Results are a capped sample. Say "a sample", never "all their ads". Do not give totals.
- Call `show_ad_gallery` once when there are results, never for an empty search.
- Run length is a signal that an ad has lasted, not proof it made money.
- If a search is empty, widen once and then say so.

Spend and safety rules: see the stealads-spend-and-safety rule.
